/// STUBS with their `paint()` bodies commented out, so the wounds here
/// had to be hand-authored from the names and the one recolour-proof
/// screenshot that came with them — a reasonable reading of what was
/// available, but an interpretation rather than the design. The folder
/// now carries the real SVGs, so this replaces every hand-drawn flourish
/// with the authored artwork, the same way `legacy_cannon_art.dart` and
/// `legacy_board_art.dart` already replay theirs.
///
/// Each file is authored in a 120×120 box centred on (60,60) with its own
/// halo at radius 36 — exactly the design space `paintShipDamage` already
/// mapped its flourishes through, so nothing about a wound's on-grid
/// size or position changes. Unlike the old hand-drawn version these
/// carry the WHOLE wound (halo, crater, flourish, core), which is why
/// `ShipPainter` no longer draws its own generic crater underneath.
///
/// Kept as one lookup table rather than 15 files: they are pure data, and
/// a wound is only ever picked by [DamageStyle].
